{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-part-reference","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0093","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The proposition labels its relevant order-preservation and monotone-limit results as parts (c) and (d); there are no parts (iii) and (iv).","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt233.tex:333-334","source_text":"By (iii) and (iv)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt233.tex:340","target_text":"Menurut (c) dan (d)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S233"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0094","math_ordinal":312,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Part (g) is about the fixed pair f_0 and g_0.  No un-subscripted f is defined in this proposition; both integrals must use f_0 to establish the stated conditional-expectation identity.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt233.tex:358-359","source_normalized_sha256":"a239ddf869969afde75c4060d714f31c7adc739fb005c961edea68cb97d4a36b","source_text":"\\int_Ff\\times\\chi F_i ... \\int_Ff\\times h","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt233.tex:367-368","target_normalized_sha256":"a9b0e7eba99602a2cc3d5372832c5a110d15d65cde8a0209737f1bec2c4cca4b","target_text":"\\int_Ff_0\\times\\chi F_i ... \\int_Ff_0\\times h","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S233"}
{"classification":"mathematical-undefined-index-range","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0095","math_ordinal":381,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The preceding statement defines b_q and hence phi_q only for q in I intersect Q.  The supremum must use that domain; the rest of the proof already does so.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt233.tex:458-459","source_normalized_sha256":"589c21155d6bd754199b0731aba21a4564e8989f1ec56571397b59511ab7a873","source_text":"\\phi(x)\\ge\\sup_{q\\in\\Bbb Q}\\phi_q(x)","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt233.tex:472-473","target_normalized_sha256":"8add8e97dca11be57e2d3856d0aef743e4145770e2a157b84ed1a389f69195b0","target_text":"\\phi(x)\\ge\\sup_{q\\in I\\cap\\Bbb Q}\\phi_q(x)","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S233"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-threshold","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0096","math_ordinal":497,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The first branch has 0<=k<4^n and therefore covers values below 2^{-n}4^n=2^n.  The constant cap branch must begin at 2^n; 2^{-n} overlaps almost the entire first branch and does not define a function.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt233.tex:590","source_normalized_sha256":"606c0a4604fb468d6dc656ed463552c3b4c6f377c2804b7aec59ead21d6ad588","source_text":"\\tilde h(x)\\ge 2^{-n}","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt233.tex:608","target_normalized_sha256":"0ea870d036063a07a26606e87a9c40cfc3d55722c2f9b1ff4867731708e3a4e2","target_text":"\\tilde h(x)\\ge 2^n","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S233"}
{"classification":"mathematical-type-error","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0097","math_ordinal":737,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The exercise calls phi convex and compares phi of the vector of integrals with the scalar integral of phi.  The immediately preceding scalar-valued convex-function results and the inequality require codomain R, not R^r.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt233.tex:812","source_normalized_sha256":"c3b979b675e2d679eca275aee52f219f5c47d3b775ecb23f37a7b53e5247dd3d","source_text":"$\\phi:C\\to\\BbbR^r$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt233.tex:849","target_normalized_sha256":"3a11aafba515bbbd2cc791402efe78d9f2ff7f06f2563a7c92417e5066c10bde","target_text":"$\\phi:C\\to\\Bbb R$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S233"}
